# Learn Go Concurrency

Learn Go concurrency from basics to production-grade patterns.

## Sections

1. **01-goroutines** - Basic goroutine usage and scheduling
2. **02-channels** - Channel communication (buffered, unbuffered, direction)
3. **03-select** - Select statement for multiplexing channels
4. **04-sync** - Synchronization primitives (Mutex, WaitGroup, atomic)
5. **05-patterns** - Common concurrency patterns (pipeline, pub/sub)
6. **06-worker-pool** - Worker pool to bound concurrency
7. **07-pipeline** - Multi-stage data processing pipeline
8. **08-fanout-fanin** - Fan-out and fan-in patterns
9. **09-semaphore** - Rate-limiting and RWMutex
10. **10-errgroup** - Propagate errors across goroutines & context cancellation

## How to Run

` + "```" + `bash
cd 01-goroutines && go run main.go
cd 06-worker-pool && go run main.go
` + "```" + `

## Key Concepts

| Pattern | Use When |
|---------|----------|
| Worker Pool | Limit concurrent goroutines doing heavy work |
| Pipeline | Transform data through sequential stages |
| Fan-out/in | Spread one stream across many workers, merge results |
| Semaphore | Limit # of goroutines accessing a resource |
| ErrGroup | First-error-wins with automatic cancellation |
